// 40 mm bolted ball: two printed hemisphere shells joined by a core disc.
// Each shell is held by one M5x20 into a hex nut captive in the core.
// The lower shell is flipped and turned 90 degrees so the two bolts cross.
plate 256 256 6
shell ← shell.coscad ×2 ▽bot
core  ← core.coscad ×1
asm = shell ⊕ core ⊕ (shell |> rotx 180 |> rotz 90)
fastener M5x20 shell#1 core rt  head=socket nut=hex pocket=top
fastener M5x20 shell#2 core bak head=socket nut=hex pocket=bot
